Give the script's directory entries a full path.

For rmdir (fltDirectories), TScript::CreateFileList makes a bare
TRemoteFile with only its name and type: no directory list, no full file
name. TWebDAVFileSystem::DeleteFile takes the path from File->FullFileName,
which, with neither set, dereferences the null directory list. Under
C++Builder that surfaces as an access violation exception, so the command
fails; elsewhere the process crashes. The entry now carries its absolute
path, resolved as TTerminal::DoDeleteFile resolves the same name. Line
counts are unchanged.

--- a/source/core/Script.cpp	2026-10-11 20:37:20.851630602 -0300
+++ b/source/core/Script.cpp	2026-10-11 20:37:33.538102140 -0300
@@ -586,7 +586,7 @@
         if (FLAGSET(ListType, fltDirectories))
         {
           TRemoteFile * File = new TRemoteFile();
-          File->FileName = FileName;
+          File->FileName = FileName; File->FullFileName = FTerminal->AbsolutePath(FileName, true); // linscp: no listing to resolve it
           File->Type = FILETYPE_DIRECTORY;
           Result->AddObject(FileName, File);
         }
